---
title: Korean Fried Chicken
source: https://www.theguardian.com/food/2021/oct/06/how-to-make-the-perfect-korean-fried-chicken-recipe
servings: 3
course: Main
prep time: 20m
cook time: 30m
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Korean
---

= Sauce =

Cook the @garlic{3%cloves} and @ginger{2%tsp}(grated) with the @oil{1%tbsp} in a #small frying pan{} until fragrant. Add the remaining sauce ingredients (@tomato ketchup{75%ml}, @gochujang (chilli paste){60%ml}, @honey or golden syrup{45%ml}, and @rice or white vinegar{1%tbsp}). Bring to a bubbling simmer, and then set aside.

= Chicken Preparation =

Mix @cornflour{2%tbsp} with @baking powder{0.5%tsp} in a bowl. Toss each @chicken wings or thighs{6}(halved) piece (divided as required) in the flour mixture. Spread on a #rack over a tray{}, and refrigerate for at least ~{30%minutes}.
Heat the #deep fat fryer{} oil to 150°C.

= Batter =

Mix the batter dry ingredients (@plain flour{75%g}, @cornflour{75%g}, @baking powder{0.5%tsp}, and @salt{0.5%tsp}) in a bowl. Add sufficient @sparkling water{200%ml} to make a loose batter with the consistency of single cream.

= Fry Chicken =

Add the chicken pieces to the batter, and stir to coat. Shake off excess batter and drop into the hot oil. Cook for 8 to ~{10%minutes} until lightly golden. Drain on a clean rack.

Skim any loose batter from the oil. Increase the temperature to 190°C.

Return the chicken pieces to the hot oil. Cook for another ~{5%minutes} until deeply golden.

Return the chicken to the rack (or place in a warm oven).

Reheat the sauce and use to coat the chicken. Transfer to a serving bowl, and scatter with the @spring onions{2} and @?sesame seeds{1%tbsp}.